WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:08.271
Zero Trust is a cybersecurity strategy based on continuously evaluating access rather than assuming trust from network location.

2
00:00:08.271 --> 00:00:15.176
The familiar shorthand is never trust, always verify, but the deeper idea is to avoid implicit trust.

3
00:00:15.176 --> 00:00:23.378
Traditional security models often placed strong controls around a network perimeter and treated activity inside that boundary as more trustworthy.

4
00:00:23.378 --> 00:00:31.899
Modern environments make that assumption less reliable because users, devices, applications, and data operate across many locations.

5
00:00:31.899 --> 00:00:36.000
Zero Trust focuses protection on resources and access decisions.

6
00:00:36.000 --> 00:00:48.621
Before allowing access, an organization evaluates who or what is requesting it, the device involved, the requested resource, current risk, applicable policy, and available security signals.

7
00:00:48.621 --> 00:00:51.385
Verification is not limited to the first sign-in.

8
00:00:51.385 --> 00:01:03.687
Conditions can change during a session: a device may fall out of compliance, an account may show unusual activity, a resource may become more sensitive, or threat information may raise concern.

9
00:01:03.687 --> 00:01:13.915
Zero Trust therefore combines identity, device posture, application controls, data protection, network visibility, policy enforcement, and monitoring.

10
00:01:13.915 --> 00:01:16.928
No single component represents the whole strategy.

11
00:01:16.928 --> 00:01:21.618
The goal is not to make work impossible or to treat every person as malicious.

12
00:01:21.618 --> 00:01:30.019
The goal is to make access explicit, appropriately limited, observable, and responsive to risk while still supporting business operations.

13
00:01:30.019 --> 00:01:33.651
Zero Trust also does not promise to eliminate cyber risk.

14
00:01:33.651 --> 00:01:44.297
It helps reduce unnecessary access, limit exposure, improve visibility, and make security decisions using stronger context than physical or network location alone.

15
00:01:44.297 --> 00:01:48.767
This course provides educational information about Zero Trust concepts.

16
00:01:48.767 --> 00:01:56.220
It is not architecture guidance, implementation advice, compliance guidance, or vendor-specific recommendation material.
